    <div class="sg-why__content">
      <span class="sg-why__eyebrow">Why Solar Gard for Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="sg-why__headline">Philadelphia's Commercial Glass Deserves Film That Documents Its Own Performance</h2>
      <p class="sg-why__intro">
        Zone 4A requires film that performs across heating and cooling seasons — and Philadelphia’s institutional buyers require film that comes with documentation to match. Solar Gard Panorama and Sentinel Plus carry NFRC-certified VLT, SHGC, and U-value ratings, giving procurement teams the third-party spec sheets required for LEED credits, GSA specifications, and school board capital approvals. For University City medical centers, Northeast Philadelphia school districts, and Center City commercial landlords, that documentation trail is often as decisive as the performance numbers themselves.
      </p>
      <ul class="sg-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
